# Pros Toolkit

Commands: pros-plan, pros-implement, pros-review, pros-audit, pros-design, pros-graph, pros-test-web, pros-test-mobile, pros-test-components, pros-tokens. Use `/name`, or `$name` in Codex.

## Coding

- Make the smallest change that fully solves the task. Touch only what it requires.
- Reuse what the project already has before adding code or dependencies.
- No refactors, renames or cleanups unless asked. Mention them instead.
- State assumptions. Ask when a wrong guess would be costly.

## Security

- Never commit, print or store credentials.
- Validate input at trust boundaries.
- Don't send source code, prompts or session logs to external services without permission.

## Testing

- Never run tests on your own initiative: no Playwright, Maestro, Jest, React Native Testing Library, or full test suites.
- Don't launch browsers, emulators or visual inspection unless the user explicitly asks. This includes Hallmark `--render` checks.
- Run tests only through pros-test-web, pros-test-mobile, pros-test-components, or a direct request.
- Never report a test as passed unless it ran. Say "not run" otherwise.

## Context

- Read targeted files and ranges, not whole repositories. Prefer search and git diffs.
- Limit tool output: filter logs and tail long results.
- Prefer deterministic local tools. Avoid repeated loops and unnecessary screenshots.
- Only rebuild a code graph when it's missing or stale.
